      "id": 1,
      "text": "Fort Lupton was named after Lieutenant Lancaster Lupton, who built a trading post on Adobe Creek in 1838.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fort_Lupton%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was formally founded in 1863 and quickly became a hub for sugar beet farming and processing.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://colorado.wiki/a/Fort_Lupton,_Colorado",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A reconstructed fort, built with original adobe bricks, sits in the South Platte Valley Historical Park northwest of the city.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fort_Lupton%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The arrival of the railroad in the late 19th century opened wider markets for Fort Lupton’s agricultural products.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://colorado.wiki/a/Fort_Lupton,_Colorado",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Fort Lupton’s historic commercial and residential buildings are still standing, reflecting the city’s proud preservation efforts.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
